WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to start
by asking you this.

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, a lot of attention
was paid to the fact

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
that when Clemson
went to the White House,

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.740 line:92%
they were served fast food.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
You commented on this
on "Good Morning America."

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had something to say
to those players.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I said --
You know what?

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.447 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I watched the game.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody expected
Alabama to win.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:19.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
What a great win for Clemson.
Dominating.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:21.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
You go to the White House
and you get burgers?

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you get fast food?
-Yeah.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:24.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I was thinking,
you know what?

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would buy
those kids lobster, man.

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:28.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
They deserve a great meal.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:32.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For a great game,
for a great season.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you ever --
Have you ever --

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.602
Were you ever lucky enough to
have a meal at the White House?

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:38.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you ever?
-Oh, we won the Super Bowl.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:42.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Famously.
Famously.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:45.912
-We stacked it with Giants fans.
Thank you very much.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Cheering ]

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
But when we won,
I had already made plans

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
for, like -- for an event.
-Yeah.

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:54.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they made the day
that we went to the Super Bowl

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
the same day as the event,
and I was trying to be

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
a man of my word,
so I skipped the White House

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that I didn't upset
the people who I committed to.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure. That makes sense.
-Yeah.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you know what
the Giants were served?

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:07.133 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Did you hear?

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have no idea,
but it wasn't fast food.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no
-I can tell you that.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:12.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was better than that, man.
But I was --

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just saw this meme
the other day, which I loved.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:18.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the President
dressed up like a Hamburglar.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:19.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if you saw that.
-Yeah.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it said, "I'm gonna make
Taco Bell pay for it."

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:24.117 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
In front of all the burgers,
and I'm like, that's --

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's good.
-Internet's undefeated.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:29.923 line:92%
-That's some good meme work.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, this is a very --
Obviously, it seems as though

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:36.663
we ended up with the four most
exciting teams this weekend.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:37.831 line:92%
Would you say that's true?

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:40.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We have the four
best offenses in the league.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:43.169
I think it's the first time ever
the four best offenses.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Highest-ranked.
-Highest-ranked have made it

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:47.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
to this point in the season.
It's gonna be exciting.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
People like points.
-Yeah.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, now, they don't
want to see defensive guys,

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
like myself,
hit quarterbacks anymore.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Now you touch one --

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
boop! -- flag.
-Absolutely.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
Absolutely.
It's tough.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.954 size:75% position:38%
I mean, I grew up --
You know, and I want

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
to talk about
being a Steeler fan,

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
but this was --
much like the Giants,

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
these were often teams
built on defense.

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a different era
we're living in right now.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:09.629 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-It's a different era.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:12.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to be able to score
30 points a game to win.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:15.502
But I do think the best defense
of all four of these teams

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
is probably the Saints.
-Yeah.

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:19.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Probably the Saints.

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's funny.
People say, "Who's gonna win?"

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:24.210
I think the Saints
are hard to beat in New Orleans.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just hard to beat.
On any other game,

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:30.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
Kansas City, talent-wise,
is the better team,

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:33.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
but for some reason,
it's like Brady and Belichick

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
have this voodoo on you.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:37.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's amazing
that they keep winning.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like,
"How does this happen?"

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.660
-Well, it's hard when you have
more talent if the other team

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
made a deal with the devil.
Like, that is --

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.631 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can't win, man.
-Historically --

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I say this --
I want to make it clear

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:52.505
that I -- I -- all my criticisms
of the Patriots

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
comes from a place
of deep jealousy.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I want them to know
I'm being petty

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.811 line:92%
because I want what they have.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.446 line:92%
You played against Tom Brady,

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:03.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now who's just
an absolutely lovely guy.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:06.052
It breaks my heart to say that.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:09.122
You are partnering with him
on a sports media company.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:12.125
What's it like sitting across
from Tom Brady in a meeting?

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's great.
It's not as comfortable

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
as laying on him
on the football field.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:19.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's great.
You hit it on the head.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.737 size:88% position:44%
When we're on the field,
we are like this, man.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:25.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:28.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But when it's over,
it's the ultimate respect.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.542 line:92%
I have so much respect for him,

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to be in this situation
that he's in now,

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:34.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
and as many Super Bowls
that's he's been in

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.482 line:92%
in his career, I'm jealous.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.618
Took me 15 years to get to two.
-Yeah.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And lose one.
This guy's been in --

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's won like five,
and he's been in like eight

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.090 size:84% position:42% line:92%
or something like that.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He goes to Super Bowls
in the summer.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:47.293 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
He has extra Super Bowls
that are happening --

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:52.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I got some spare time.
Let me go to a Super Bowl.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the guy,
he's absolutely amazing.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's a great business partner,
because as hard as he works

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:57.904 line:92%
to be a great football player,

00:03:57.904 --> 00:04:00.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
he works that hard
off the field, as well,

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.675
in our business, which is called
Religion of Sports,

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we do
all these great documentaries

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.012 line:92%
and a lot of branded content.

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:08.781
We did "Tom versus Time,"
was something we did last year,

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:13.253
but we followed last season
for him because he is 41 now.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:16.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Like, the clock is ticking.

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this guy
continues to defy age.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:20.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
He is a well-made clock.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a bummer.
-But there's nothing

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
like hitting a quarterback
like Brady, man.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.699
-Yeah.
-Whoo! Gisele, I see why, girl.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:29.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
I see why!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:33.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just contact.
How --

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:37.010
It seems -- If there was a
positive in the Giants' season,

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there were a few,
Saquon Barkley.

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:40.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-There was some criticism.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you not take
a quarterback

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:44.450
in last year's draft?
It seems like this is a pick now

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.352
that you can stand by and say
this was the right choice.

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.821
-You can stand by and say
he was the right choice.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.323 line:92%
I mean, the kid is phenomenal.

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:51.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the quarterback,
it's a hit-or-miss thing.

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:53.993
I think he was pretty much
a hit from the beginning.

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:55.662
-Yeah.
-You knew what you were getting.

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:58.598
This year, there are not as many
quarterbacks in the draft,

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:01.301 size:88% position:44%
but I do think you can
find somebody, possibly,

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:03.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
to sit behind Eli
most of the year.

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:03.670 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yep.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.738
-And hopefully maybe free agency
or something like that.

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:09.142
But I think if you protect Eli,
he can get you far enough

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.444
to blend somebody else in
to take over eventually.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:14.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm heartbroken.
We talked a little backstage.

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:16.749 line:92%
The Steelers had a year --

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.851
Any time they don't make
the playoffs, I'm very sad.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:21.954
I'm sad most of the time
if they don't win a Super Bowl.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they had this drama
with Le'Veon Bell all year.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
Finally get past it,
and now there seems to be

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:28.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
this new drama
with Antonio Brown.

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's been no player
I've enjoyed watching more

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:33.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the last decade
on the Steelers than him.

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But this seems --

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it safe to say
this is a marriage

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:38.271 line:92%
that is not going to end well?

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:40.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think if you're gonna root
for Antonio Brown,

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:41.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
you'll be rooting
for another team.

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:43.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause I just don't think
he's gonna be there next year.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
Too much of a distraction.
-Yeah.

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:47.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they've had enough of it
with Le'Veon Bell,

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:49.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he decided
he didn't want to come back,

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:50.650 line:92%
and they kind of moved on.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
Too much to do that
year after year

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:53.986 line:92%
and expect your team to compete.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Were wide receivers
always like this?

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:58.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're divas, man!
-Yeah.

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:00.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Even in your era.

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:05.164
-Like, you know, and that's why
you need a player on the team

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:08.368
who can go up and grab them
and say, "Hey, get it together."

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:09.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know, "You got to

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:10.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
get it together.
You're hurting us."

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.474
-The problem is, Antonio's so
fast, he's impossible to grab.

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:15.007 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even when they try to grab him
and tell him that, voom!

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:20.480
-You lock the locker-room doors,
he ain't going nowhere.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.381 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:23.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'll be heartbroken
to see him leave,

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:25.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it certainly doesn't seem
very positive right now.

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:26.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
Always great to see you.
-Always, my friend!

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:28.755 line:92%
-Thank you for being here.

